{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-sequence_algorithms-typescript-repair-01","problem":"Repair the source below and return one complete TypeScript source file.

The file must export exactly the declared `LogEntry`, `PageOptions`, and `rankWindow` API. `rankWindow` sorts all entries by `score` in the requested direction, then returns the half-open window beginning at `offset` and containing at most `limit` entries. Callers provide non-negative integer pagination values, finite scores, and distinct scores.

The function must not mutate `entries`. Every returned entry must also be a new object, so changing a returned entry cannot change an input entry. Do not use filesystem, network, clock, randomness, packages, or frameworks.

The current implementation incorrectly changes caller-owned state:

```typescript
export interface LogEntry {
  key: string;
  score: number;
  payload: string;
}

export interface PageOptions {
  offset: number;
  limit: number;
  direction: "asc" | "desc";
}

export function rankWindow(
  entries: LogEntry[],
  options: PageOptions,
): LogEntry[] {
  const factor = options.direction === "asc" ? 1 : -1;
  entries.sort((left, right) => factor * (left.score - right.score));

  return entries
    .slice(options.offset, options.offset + options.limit)
    .map((entry) => ({ ...entry }));
}
```","reference_code":"export interface LogEntry {
  key: string;
  score: number;
  payload: string;
